  <div class="sh">✦ Final Summary ✦</div>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;"><strong>§§69–70</strong>: <em>Birchas HaMazon</em> = drawing <em>Ratzon</em> through speech. <em>Shemo</em> = <em>Ratzon</em>. Three <em>berachos</em>: (1) Moshe → <em>mah</em>/upper; (2) Yehoshua → <em>Eretz Yisrael</em>/lower; (3) Dovid & Shlomo → <em>Boneh Yerushalayim</em>/inclusiveness.</p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;"><strong>§71</strong>: <em>HaTov V'HaMeitiv</em> = fourth <em>berachah</em> = World to Come. Burial of the slain of Beitar = beginning of eternal life. After the destruction, we draw <em>Ratzon</em> from the future through this added <em>berachah</em>.</p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;"><strong>§72</strong>: Yirmiyahu: "They are new every morning" = <em>techiyas hameisim</em>. Now we must strengthen in <em>Ratzon</em> even more.</p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;"><strong>§73</strong>: <em>Bein HaMetzarim</em>. All destruction from <em>machlokes</em>. <em>Mah</em> became <em>lanu</em> (ego). "Not to us — but to Your Name give glory."</p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;"><strong>§§74–76</strong>: <em>Zimun</em> = expressing <em>Ratzon</em> aloud: "<em>mir villen bentshen!</em>" Three = three <em>Kedushos</em>. Ten = mentioning the Name, because <em>Ayeh</em> to <em>Melo</em> = ten <em>Sefiros</em>.</p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;"><strong>§77</strong>: <em>Makifin</em>. The <em>tzadik</em> ascends through free choice; the angel stands still. "The end of knowledge is that we do not know." <em>Rabbainu</em>: where philosophy ends, true <em>Kabbalah</em> begins — and even there, ascent continues.</p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;"><strong>§78</strong>: Moshe's departure = Yehoshua's empowerment. "Greater are the <em>tzadikim</em> in death." Through one synagogue returning in truth, <em>Mashiach</em> will come.</p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;"><strong>§79</strong>: "<em>Nachamu</em>" = comfort one another. Three <em>Aichahs</em>: exile, destruction, departure of the <em>tzadik</em>. "A voice calls in the wilderness" — no despair. "Every valley raised, every mountain lowered." "The glory of Hashem shall be revealed."</p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:.8rem;"><strong>§§80–84</strong>: 15 Av = Yom Kippur = <em>tikkun</em> of <em>meraglim</em>. <em>Eikev</em> = even at the heel, if you heed the <em>da'as</em>. "Do not fear — Hashem fights for you." The <em>minyan</em> derived from the <em>meraglim</em> — from the evil assembly, Hashem taught us holy assemblies. <strong>The counsel of Hashem stands forever.</strong></p>
